Q: Non-existent parameter from private bundle while loading extension twig A: <p>Setting parameter in the builder seems to affect only the current bundle but If I do :</p>
<pre><code>class SoCoreBundle extends AbstractBundle {
public function loadExtension(array $config, ContainerConfigurator $container, ContainerBuilder $builder): void {
$container-&gt;parameters()
    -&gt;set('so_core.routing', $config['routing']);
...
</code></pre>
<p>It's ok and twig found it.</p>

Q: Deprecation of dynamodb_table in Terraform S3 Backend A: <p>That should be listed somewhere in the terraform documentation. If not, you can still limit the version of terraform you use with version pinning, something like:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>terraform {
  required_version = &quot;= x.x.x&quot; # replace the x.x.x with the version supporting DynamoDB
}
</code></pre>
<p>After the version in which it will stop working is announced, you can then make the change permanent and remove the version pinning.</p>
